Docker Image Build & Runtime Check	Build image	2026-08-15T17:36:58.9627311Z             "body": "## Summary\n\n- Treat a self-development-policy-ineligible automatic release as a clean\n  deferral while retaining the strict manual release gate.\n- Build the all-feature macOS nextest archive once, then fan it out to three\n  bounded partition runners instead of compiling the graph three times.\n- Add one fail-closed gate that discovers and audits every committed Bun/npm\n  lock; upgrade DOMPurify and the vulnerable Puppeteer extraction chains until\n  all five live locks report zero advisories.\n- Remove misleading Gemini true-color/project-lock warnings and Bun lifecycle\n  noise, and rename archived manifests so Dependency Graph cannot treat\n  historical evidence as live applications.\n- Preserve the complete issue/PR/CI evidence, reconstructed timeline, nine\n  requirements, root-cause ledger, template comparison, and upstream reports.\n\n## Root causes and reproduction\n\nThe issue-listed baseline contained one real Auto Release failure, which\nPipeline Status correctly propagated. The new hard self-development gate ran\nafter an immutable release cycle without a qualifying PR, so every future\nautomatic run would stay red even though retrying could not change eligibility.\nThe macOS warnings were also real: all three nextest slices rebuilt the same\nall-feature graph before partitioning. Install-time npm audit output did not\nfail CI, leaving four vulnerable dependency surfaces behind an apparent green\nrun.\n\nThe tests-first commit `769c1eac` captures the seven initial failures. The\ncanonical evidence index contains all twelve named baseline run logs, all five\ninitial PR run logs, run/job/artifact metadata, 66 check-annotation responses,\nall three PR discussion surfaces, and the red/green reproduction:\n\n[`dev/log/issues/1014/pulls/1015/README.md`](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-1014-fa915643117e/dev/log/issues/1014/pulls/1015/README.md)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --test unit -- ci_cd::issue_1014` — 12/12 pass\n- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features`\n- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo check --examples --all-features`\n- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo test --all-features --verbose` — 2,804 library\n  tests plus every integration binary pass\n- `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings cargo test --doc --all-features --verbose`\n- `bash scripts/check-javascript-dependencies.sh` — all five locks clean\n- desktop tests — 140/140; VS Code tests — 51/51; web tests — 75/75 plus build\n- actionlint with the repository's documented `queue` schema exception\n- formatting, diff whitespace, shell syntax, changelog, static policies, and\n  committed-range secret scan (351 files)\n\nFull local output is retained under\n`dev/log/issues/1014/pulls/1015/local-tests/`. Fresh GitHub runs are verified by\ntimestamp and exact head SHA before this draft is marked ready.\n\n## Upstream reports\n\n- [Gemini CLI #28826](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/28826)\n- [web-capture #153](https://github.com/link-assistant/web-capture/issues/153)\n- [html-to-markdown #459](https://github.com/xberg-io/html-to-markdown/issues/459)\n- [Rust pipeline template #132](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/132)\n- [JavaScript pipeline template #134](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/134)\n- [Python pipeline template #58](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/58)\n\nFixes #1014\n",
